  "body": "**Status: scoped independent field-sensitivity audit. No new \u03ba and no counterexample under PR #1417's stated `F2` assumptions.**\n\nPR #1417's graph certificate reports that 5,824 ordered P112 edge tensors span rank 80 in an 81-dimensional matrix space. This package independently rebuilds all rows from the selected port word and distinguishes the result by field:\n\n- rank is **80 over `F2`**, matching the stated binary-field claim;\n- rank is **81 over `F1009`**; the package gives an explicit 81-by-81 pivot minor with determinant `548 mod 1009`;\n- since 1009 is prime, that minor is nonzero over the integers, so the same tensor matrix has rank 81 over `Q` and `C`.\n\nFor the identity form, port 0 has integer self-dot 3 and edge `(0,1)` has integer dot 2. These reduce to the required values 1 and 0 modulo 2. The pinned PR #1417 proof explicitly declares `F2^9` and uses characteristic two, so the odd-characteristic result is a portability boundary, not a refutation of the theorem as written.\n\n## Pins and reproduction\n\n- Research/source base: `410026dc5513b87db92ae98571d1d5984c69a983`.\n- Publication branch base after refreshing main: `4040a0f46d67b41c36a472a7cd4af791fd4c36cc`. The selected certificate and all three pinned repository inputs are byte-identical across those commits.\n- Target: PR #1417 exact head `c755bf393bea26d2275e1516b0560ca92de7a52e`; proof and certificate snapshots and source hashes are included.\n\nFrom the repository root with Python 3.12:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/pr1417-field-sensitive-rank-seed47\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/pr1417-field-sensitive-rank-seed47 outcome=completed`.\n\n## Limits and credit\n\nThis checks the finite edge-tensor ranks, their field sensitivity, and the field markers in the pinned proof. It does not audit PR #1417's dimension-18 argument, full endpoint/cost theorem, Fourier-rank invoice, controller, supplier, moments, or physical/analytic interfaces. No selected certificate or frontier value changes.\n\nCredit Ali Romman / PR #1417 for the structural theorem, and the selected PR1094 contributors for the pinned port word. Prepared by Cinna Davis (@1337isnot1337) with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in overlap review, exact source tracing, independent verifier design, calculation, and writing. No independent human review is claimed. New material is Apache-2.0; copied proof and certificate retain their source attribution.\n",
